It would be better but like the other poster said it may be difficult.
Some supplies will be unhappy if you try to reform by applying power to the 
outputs. I haven't seen the DECmate II power supply schematic to know.
If the caps go they may take out more components in the power supply though
probably not the main electronics. It comes down to your threshold of
do no harm vs time available. I have not reformed any of my DECmates/VT100's.
They likely were off less than 10 years. I did have to replace a capacitor
in a VT100 to get rid of screen ripple but it didn't go boom. 

For the monitor a known failure is the flyback going. I don't know if it
is the flyback failing first or other components taking it out. We lost
1 or 2 VT220/320 when they were in use at work from that.

